# Algorithmic Counseling. University of Minnesota Education Career Development Office R.&D. Report No. 1976-3.

**Authors:** Hummel, Thomas J.

## Abstract
"Algorithmic counseling" is an attempt to apply recent instructional regulation techniques to graduate counselor training and research. This paper seeks to explain what algorithms are, why they could be useful, and how they can be constructed. A central motivation for studying algorithms is their utility in showing students how to accomplish a task in specific, completely understandable steps. The paper includes an algorithm designed to reflect client feelings. (Author)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=ED136160

